  <title>RMDIR Command</title>
  <keywords>
    <keyword>Commands</keyword>
    <keyword>Files and folders</keyword>
    <keyword>RMDIR command</keyword>
    <keyword>RD command</keyword>
  </keywords>
  <body>
    <header>
      <para styleclass="Heading1">RMDIR | RD Command</para>
    </header>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><snippet src="__FoxProOnly" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><snippet src="__CommandInclude" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Purpose</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">Removes an empty folder.</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Syntax</para>
    <para styleclass="Code with box">RMDIR | RD &lt;FolderName&gt;</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Arguments</para>
    <para styleclass="List">&lt;FolderName&gt;<tab />The name of the folder to remove. The name may be specified with or without quotes.</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Remarks</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">RD is a synonym for RMDIR. The folder must be empty: the command does not remove the files and sub folders inside the folder. An error is generated when the folder cannot be removed.</para>
    <para styleclass="Body Text"><snippet src="__IncludeLibVFP" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">See Also</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_MKDIR">MKDIR</link>, <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_CHDIR">CHDIR</link>, <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_DIR">DIR</link></para>
  </body>
